                <pb facs="1555" n="1380" xml:id="pg1380"/>

                <head>507. NSC Executive Committee record of
                    action, November 8<anchor n="1" xml:id="d507-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <idno type="document-identifier">Meeting No. 23</idno>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1962-11-08T16:30:00">November 8, 1962, 4:30
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d507-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d507-1"/>
                <p>1. A press release was discussed and approved which summarizes our current
                    knowledge of the removal from Cuba of Soviet missiles and related equipment.</p>
                <p>2. There was a discussion of: (a) long-term surveillance requirements; (b)
                    courses of action in the event a U.S. reconnaissance plane is shot at or
                    destroyed; and (c) ways to keep pressure on Castro other than by reinstituting
                    the quarantine.</p>
                <p>3. Secretary McNamara reported there was
                    no reaction to today’s aerial reconnaissance mission. Tomorrow’s missions were
                    authorized comprising five U–2 flights and ten
                    low-level flights.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed corresp="#p_BM_1">McGeorge
                        Bundy</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
